AI Behavioral Auditor: The Mathematical Guardian of Autonomous Lunar Infrastructure

ouadi Maakoul 

AI : chatGpt, Deepseek, Gemini 

Abstract 

As humanity expands beyond Earth, autonomous systems will manage life‑critical infrastructure in environments where communication delays preclude real‑time terrestrial oversight. The lunar colony of 2058—with 12 000 humans, 1.8 million AI agents, and 340 000 robots—serves as the paradigmatic use case. The “AI Behavioral Auditor” is an emergent profession combining applied mathematics, systems engineering, and formal methods. This paper defines the profession’s core mission—to mathematically prove the continued trustworthy behavior of deployed autonomous systems—and sets out the mathematical layers, a hierarchical auditing architecture, fault‑tolerant override protocols, and the educational pathways required. In response to the challenges of scalability, deceptive alignment, and cyber‑physical uncertainty, the blueprint is deepened with compositional verification, latent‑space monitoring, causal disentanglement, and a cryptographically enforced meta‑shield that turns ethical dilemmas into formally decidable optimisation problems.

