The AI Behavioral Auditor is not an IT position. It is an applied mathematics discipline and a safety‑critical engineering profession that acts as the immune system of a civilisation built on intelligence. By layering compositional verification, causal uncertainty bounding, mechanistic interpretability, and a cryptographically enforced conflict‑resolution protocol, the blueprint resolves the core paradoxes of scalability, deception, and environmental chaos. As autonomous systems become the critical infrastructure of a multiplanetary economy, the ability to mathematically measure, verify, monitor, and constrain artificial intelligence—under bounded knowledge and adversarial pressure—will become as essential as civil engineering was during the Industrial Revolution. The profession not only assures safety; it encodes the ethical primacy of human life in the only language that a superhuman intelligence must obey: formal mathematical proof.


